  "packageHash": "JVkAfB8ya1bjzYHUNpr3vq2edwFawu8W+jFHH+lixvDr+4jvuQ/H9kruK8Mb4oq9K/wRS+Fu3DzZWzEWURFS8A==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 100817,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/tree/master/src/Abblix.SharedSignals.Redis",
  "published": "2026-09-05T11:13:29.367Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A transmitter that runs as more than one replica needs a queue that every replica sees the same way. This outbox keeps each stream's pending events in Redis list and hash structures and performs enqueue, claim and acknowledge as atomic server-side operations, so two replicas cannot deliver the same event twice or lose one between them - which a queue over a plain distributed cache cannot promise. Drop-in for the default in-process outbox. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v2.4",
  "repository": {
    "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.09.05.11.16.37/abblix.sharedsignals.redis.2.4.0.json#repository",
